Wire fixtures — provenance & integrity
======================================

The *.sse files in ./wire are VERBATIM Server-Sent Event byte streams in the
Anthropic Messages streaming format. They are the permanent, offline RECORD
source for cassette's self-tests and the north-star demo: the in-process fake
provider (internal/fakeprovider) replays these exact bytes over httptest so the
real Anthropic SDK decoder consumes them just as it would a live stream.

Provenance
----------
No live API key or network was used (none is available, by design). These
streams were HAND-TRANSCRIBED from the documented Anthropic Messages streaming
event sequence:

  message_start
  content_block_start
  ( ping )
  content_block_delta   (text_delta | input_json_delta)
  content_block_stop
  message_delta
  message_stop

and the documented mid-stream `error` event. Reference: Anthropic "Streaming
Messages" documentation (event/data SSE framing, text_delta and
input_json_delta deltas, ping keep-alives, and error events).

The coffee_turn_NN.sse fixtures are the six turns of a REAL multi-tool agent
conversation (five sequential tool_use calls — list_menu, get_price,
check_inventory, caffeine_mg, brew_minutes — then a final recommendation),
CAPTURED from a real provider streaming session (via a corporate LLM proxy) and
committed verbatim after secret scrubbing. They contain real model output but no
credentials.

Why these are embedded (not under testdata/wire)
------------------------------------------------
Go's //go:embed cannot reach a sibling testdata/ directory, and the runnable
demo binary (examples/) must read these fixtures offline regardless of working
directory. Embedding them in this package makes them a single source of truth
shared by the fake provider, the tests, and the demo. See DECISIONS.md.

Integrity
---------
These files are intentionally NOT happy-path-only: they include ping/comment
lines, a multibyte UTF-8 character (🌍 / é), fragmented tool-call arguments, and
a mid-stream error. The fake provider additionally writes them with adversarial
chunk boundaries (mid-event, multibyte-internal) to exercise the SDK scanner and
the streaming capture tee. They contain no secrets.
